      "side": 1,
      "message": "It would be a bit cleaner if this block, along with the definitions of the board strings, went into a function called `get_chip` and that function called `get_board`. This would look something like this:\n\n\n```\nget_board()\n{\n  local board\n  board\u003d\"$(cros_config /fingerprint board)\"\n\n  echo \"${board}\"\n}\n\nget_chip()\n{\n  if ! board\u003d\"$(get_board)\"; then\n    echo \"Failed to get board\" \u003e\u00262\n    exit \"${EXIT_CONFIG}\"\n  fi\n\n  if [[ \"${board}\" \u003d\u003d \"${HELIPILOT_STR}\" ]]; then\n    chip_type\u003d\"NPCX\"\n  elif [[ \"${board}\" \u003d\u003d \"${BLOONCHIPPER_STR}\" ]]; then\n    chip_type\u003d\"STM32\"\n  elif [[ \"${board}\" \u003d\u003d \"${DARTMONKEY_STR}\" ]]; then\n    chip_type\u003d\"STM32\"\n  else\n    echo \"ERROR: Unknown board type found: ${board}.\" \u003e\u00262\n    exit \"${EXIT_CONFIG}\"\n    \n  echo \"${chip_type}\"\n}\n\n...\n\n  board\u003d\"$(get_chip)\"\n\n  local ret\n  flash_fp_mcu \\\n    \"${TRANSPORT}\"   \\\n    \"${DEVICE}\"      \\\n    \"${GPIO_NRST}\"   \\\n    \"${GPIO_BOOT0}\"  \\\n    \"${GPIO_PWREN}\"  \\\n    \"${filename}\"    \\\n    \"${chip_type}\"\n  ret\u003d$?\n\n```",
